{
  /*
   * The IndexedDB adapter — the half of L0 storage that knows it is in a
   * browser.
   *
   * IndexedDB, BroadcastChannel and the quota estimate live here and nowhere
   * else. This is the line `check-platform.mjs` always intended: the port
   * (`Driver`), the store catalogue, the migration table and the two
   * platform-free implementations are in `@jojo/service/storage`, compiled with
   * no DOM at all, and everything on this side is allowed to name a browser
   * because naming the browser is its job.
   *
   * WHAT CHANGED WHEN THE PACKAGE SPLIT
   *
   * This project used to be `composite` with `emitDeclarationOnly`, and the
   * reason was `repo`: it imports four files out of storage, so storage was
   * reachable from a project compiled with `"lib": ["ES2023"]`, and TypeScript
   * type-checks everything it reaches. The composite emit meant `repo` saw a
   * .d.ts instead of `idb-driver.ts`, which put the DOM on the other side of a
   * declaration file.
   *
   * `repo` is in `@jojo/service` now, and its reference points at
   * `service/tsconfig.storage.json`. Nothing in this repo reaches INTO this
   * directory except the web app itself, which has DOM anyway. So the emit has
   * no consumer and is gone; this is a plain type-check project again.
   *
   * It still does not get `types`. vite/client and @types/node would let a
   * driver reach for `import.meta.env` or `fs`, and a storage adapter that can
   * read the filesystem is the Electron rewrite arriving early and by accident.
   */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.adapters.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.storage.tsbuildinfo",
    "lib": ["ES2023", "DOM"],
    "types": []
  },
  "include": ["src/kg/storage"]
}
